{#- A score histogram's Summary cell: n, mean and sd, one labelled line
    each, as `moments_summary()` formats them.  Empty when the histogram
    has no moments -- categorical, null, or stored before the
    accumulators (gain#1589).  Expects `hist` in the including scope.

    The lines do not wrap, and the score tables are `table-layout: fixed`,
    so the column cannot grow to fit them: the including table sizes its
    Summary `<col>` in pixels, not a percentage -- 200px holds a
    14-character n beside its label. #}
<td>
{%- set lines = hist.moments_summary() %}
{%- if lines %}
<dl class="moments">
{%- for label, value in lines %}
<dt>{{ label }}</dt><dd>{{ value }}</dd>
{%- endfor %}
</dl>
{%- endif -%}
</td>
